  <running_head>CANTICI</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">CANTICI</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">Sulamithis cernitur?</l>
    <l n="3">Nempe quales, horrido-</l>
    <l n="4">Præcinente classico,</l>
    <l n="5">Prodeuntes ordine-</l>
    <l n="6">Duplices &amp; hinc &amp; hinc-</l>
    <l n="7">Militum ruunt chori.</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="2" para="true">ODE. VII.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">1. Quàm tui sunt belluliQuàm</l>
    <l n="10">tui nit rtibus-</l>
    <l n="11">Calceis venustuli-</l>
    <l n="12">Sunt pedes, ô principis-</l>
    <l n="13">Præpotentis filia!</l>
    <l n="14">Sic teres fuæ femur-</l>
    <l n="15">Iunctum adhæret tibiæ,</l>
    <l n="16">Vt columnæ ceu basi-</l>
    <l n="17">Infitum scapum putes,</l>
    <l n="18">Quem peritus undique-</l>
    <l n="19">Circinarit artifex.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">2. Qualis est crater teres-</l>
    <l n="21">Temperata porrigens-</l>
    <l n="22">Haurienti pocula,</l>
    <l n="23">Talis umbiliculus-</l>
    <l n="24">Est tibi rotundulus,</l>
    <l n="25">Ventris area situs,</l>
    <l n="26">Area quæ tritici-</l>
    <l n="27">Est acervus messium:</l>
    <l n="28">Area quæ liliis-</l>
    <l n="29">Est odoris confita.</l>
    <l n="30" para="true">3. Educandis at tuis-</l>
    <l n="31">Bina spectans vbera,</l>
    <l n="32">Caprææ te comparo,</l>
    <l n="33" para="true">Gemello capreolo pulcrè Est dicata principum-</l>
    <l n="34">Nasus est decens tibi,</l>
    <l n="35">Rectus assurgens, velut-</l>
    <l n="36">Turris illa Libani,</l>
    <l n="37">Quae Damascum respicit.</l>
    <l n="38">5 Corpus hoc supra, caput-</l>
    <l n="39">Montis instar Carmel-</l>
    <l n="40">iFertur alte, coccina-</l>
    <l n="41">Erubescens rania:</l>
    <l n="42">Fulgidam mitra comam-</l>
    <l n="43">Purpurante splendida:</l>
    <l n="44">Regis in te lumina-</l>
    <l n="45">Versa quae sic detinent,</l>
    <l n="46">Ut suae folaria-</l>
    <l n="47">Alligaris regiae.</l>
    <l n="48">6. Ecquis iftud deniqu-</l>
    <l n="49">eComprehenderit decus?</l>
    <l n="50">Quis leporem, &amp; gratii-</l>
    <l n="51">sGratiores gratias?</l>
    <l n="52">7 Palma qualis edito-</l>
    <l n="53">Fertur alta vertice,</l>
    <l n="54">Celsa talis emines,</l>
    <l n="55">Plena succi praeferens,</l>
    <l n="56">Ceu racemos: vbera.</l>
    <l n="57">&amp; Ergo fixu hoc est mihi,</l>
    <l n="58">Palma in iftam scandere,</l>
    <l n="59">Hofque ramos prendere:</l>
    <l n="60">Detur iftas ut mihi-</l>
    <l n="61">Quas geris papillulas-</l>
    <l n="62">Ceu botros exfugere,</l>
    <l n="63">Nariumque pascere-</l>
    <l n="64">Me tuarum spiritu,</l>
    <l n="65">Nulla quo fragrantius</l>
    <l n="66">Quae gemellos ninnulos,</l>
    <l n="67">Comptulos, politulos,</l>
    <l n="68">Pascit inter lilia.</l>
    <l n="69">4. Lactea haec cervicula,</l>
    <l n="70">Turris est eburnea.</l>
    <l n="71">Haec tuae pupillulae,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Right column, top: "Vitreæ sunt balneæ, / Arte quales maxima / Fabricatas prospicit / Porta quæ subsellliis" (four lines, set in a separate block at the top right of the page). The last line of the scan is cut off at the bottom edge. The left column of the lower part is only partly legible; the lines are set in parallel columns and the bottom-left lines are transcribed as they appear. Catchword "Malu" at lower right is partly visible and left unread.</notes>
